! Surfaces: the areas of the polygons reproduce the xlsx areas of raw_data columns F, J and K.
! Dimensions: the xlsx (Building Summary) gives 1 floor; NREL PDF Table 13: Primary School 73,960 ft2 (6,871 m2), E-shape, 1 floor, floor-to-floor and floor-to-ceiling height 13 ft (3.96 m); the xlsx raw_data total is 6,871 m2. The positions and sizes of the rooms (the zone origins and the vertices, relative to the zone origins) are dimensions of the prototype, written in whole metres (the height of the zones is 4 m); they are not in the documents.
! Dimensions used in the vertex comments: every zone is a box. w = the width of the floor (X), d = its depth (Y) and h = the height of the zone (Z); the vertices are relative to the zone origin (the Zone objects give the origins), X to the east, Y to the north, Z up.
! The lengths are whole metres of the prototype; they are not in the documents. For a rectangular floor w x d is the floor area of the zone in the xlsx (raw_data, Area [m2]); h is near the floor-to-ceiling height of the PDF (13 ft x 0.3048 = 3.96 m). The windows lie on the walls, 0.05 m inside the wall edges, and their height gives the window glass area of the xlsx (raw_data).
  BuildingSurface:Detailed,
    Corner_Class_1_Pod_1_ZN_1_FLR_1_Wall_1,!- Name
    Wall,                         !- Surface Type
    ExteriorWall,                 !- Construction Name
    Corner_Class_1_Pod_1_ZN_1_FLR_1,!- Zone Name
    ,                             !- Space Name
    Outdoors,                     !- Outside Boundary Condition
    ,                             !- Outside Boundary Condition Object
    ,                             !- Sun Exposure
    ,                             !- Wind Exposure
    ,                             !- View Factor to Ground
    ,                             !- Number of Vertices
    0,0,4,                        !- X,Y,Z ==> Vertex 1 {m}  Derived from: X = 0 (zone origin); Y = 0 (zone origin); Z = h = 4 m.
    0,0,0,                        !- X,Y,Z ==> Vertex 2 {m}  Derived from: X = 0 (zone origin); Y = 0 (zone origin); Z = 0 (zone origin).
    11,0,0,                       !- X,Y,Z ==> Vertex 3 {m}  Derived from: X = w = 11 m; Y = 0 (zone origin); Z = 0 (zone origin).
    11,0,4;                       !- X,Y,Z ==> Vertex 4 {m}  Derived from: X = w = 11 m; Y = 0 (zone origin); Z = h = 4 m.

